\\in I}{S}_{i} & ={S}_{5}\\cup {S}_{6}\\cup {S}_{7} \\\\  & =[5,6)\\,\\cup \\,[6,7)\\,\\cup \\,[7,8) \\\\  & =[5,8).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284717 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186284037 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284717 #edb/ref 1069 "q-174447" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284717 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284717 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $I=Z$ and ${X}_{i}={i-1,\\,i},$ then ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284717 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f5b989ff-c36c-5cd1-a2e7-3a722d88ff08" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284717 #edb/ref 1074 "The intersection of a family of indexed sets ${{A}_{i}}_{i\\in I}$ contains all elements that belong to *all* sets in our family:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\in U\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for all }{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nLet's now write down a few instances of our indexed sets:\n\n- if $i=-1,$ we have ${X}_{-1}={-2,-1}$\n\n- if $i=0,$ we have ${X}_{0}={-1,0}$\n\n- if $i=1,$ we have ${X}_{1}={0,1}$\n\nand so on. \n\nNotice that there is no element that belongs to all the sets. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}=∅.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284719 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186284197 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284719 #edb/ref 1069 "q-174450" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284719 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284719 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $I=N$ and ${X}_{i}={-i,\\,0,\\,i},$ then ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284719 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2fd30642-b32d-59fc-bea9-4c1cd84ef2fd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284719 #edb/ref 1074 "The union of a family of indexed sets is the set containing all elements belonging to *at least one* set in the indexed family:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\in U\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one }{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I}\n$$\n\nwhe