igned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1+3t \\\\ 3+t \\\\ 2+3t\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ And finally, the parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1+3t \\\\ y=3+t \\\\ z=2+3t\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312025 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312025 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312025 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "077cc4da-3c12-5749-87e3-9136fa56ff18" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312445 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312445 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312445 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "39d686df-f396-5c82-92b8-3b075c274d61" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312607 #edb/ref 1080 "-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312607 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312607 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4dd5ec6b-997e-5c4c-82cd-f74e85dcbdf1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312909 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312909 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312909 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7578cf04-a90c-5b5d-ac09-511fd3e57a8d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313868 #edb/ref 1080 "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313868 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313868 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "eced6632-dc68-59a9-a39d-d5b16448d6d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314396 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186312025 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314396 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186312445 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314396 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186312607 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314396 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186312909 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314396 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186313868 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314396 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314396 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314396 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186312909 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314396 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "901fd7a3-f614-5740-8413-9326f82935f3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314972 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186314396 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314972 #edb/ref 1069 "q-34058" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314972 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314972 #edb/ref 1071 "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314972 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "dffa9b37-7313-5190-ae5f-372cf9f5aaea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314972 #edb/ref 1074 "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}=1 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}=1 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=1.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-1=1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=2\\cdot 1=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315285 #edb/ref 1080 "-8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315285 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315285 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1d12c5f6-3b92-5441-a0fc-3952c1a70749" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315374 #edb/ref 1080 "16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315374 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315374 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2be071fa-e50f-5e15-af2e-800d12bec8db" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315491 #edb/ref 1080 "-16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315491 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315491 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "40c87c4f-e4ad-5573-b56b-bbf8371657d9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315762 #edb/ref 1080 "-4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315762 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315762 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "719e49b9-6453-5c6f-ae8b-fb5f2080b954" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316048 #edb/ref 1080 "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316048 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316048 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a449e927-6b10-5f40-a19c-fccc1dc264eb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1